{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));a=r['artifacts'][0]\np=json.load(open(a['plan_path']));print('fixed plan properties:',json.dumps(p['observable_properties']));print('monitor admission:',p['monitors'][0]['admission_alias'])\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nfor b in s['bindings']:\n if b['id'] in ['BIND_append_issue','BIND_append_consume','BIND_unstable_retire'] and b['version']==1:\n  print(b['id'],b['file'],b['start_line'],b['end_line'],b['symbol'])\nPY\nsed -n '315,321p' ../agent-source/rawnode.go\nsed -n '1158,1195p' ../agent-source/raft.go\nsed -n '134,160p' ../agent-source/log_unstable.go\"","aggregated_output":"fixed plan properties: [{\"checker_id\": \"CHK_no_old_term_retirement\", \"kind\": \"event_assertion\", \"trigger\": {\"field\": \"event\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": \"completion_consumed\", \"reference\": null}, \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"offset\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": null, \"reference\": \"admitted.offset\"}, \"antecedent\": null, \"identity_fields\": [\"operation\", \"node\"], \"history_field\": null, \"description\": \"For the admitted obsolete entry-only completion with matching entry identity, the unstable offset after actual Step equals its observed offset immediately before Step.\"}]\nmonitor admission: admitted\nBIND_append_issue rawnode.go 268 365 newStorageAppendRespMsg\nBIND_append_consume raft.go 1085 1262 Step\nBIND_unstable_retire log_unstable.go 134 160 stableTo\n\t\t// To prevent these kinds of problems, we also attach the current term to the\n\t\t// MsgStorageAppendResp (above). If the term has changed by the time the\n\t\t// MsgStorageAppendResp if returned, the response is ignored and the unstable\n\t\t// log is not truncated. The unstable log is only truncated when the term has\n\t\t// remained unchanged from the time that the MsgStorageAppend was sent to the\n\t\t// time that the MsgStorageAppendResp is received, indicating that no-one else\n\t\t// is in the process of truncating the stable log.\n\t\t} else if m.Type == pb.MsgStorageAppendResp {\n\t\t\tif m.Index != 0 {\n\t\t\t\t// Don't consider the appended log entries to be stable because\n\t\t\t\t// they may have been overwritten in the unstable log during a\n\t\t\t\t// later term. See the comment in newStorageAppendResp for more\n\t\t\t\t// about this race.\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [term: %d] ignored entry appends from a %s message with lower term [term: %d]\",\n\t\t\t\t\tr.id, r.Term, m.Type, m.Term)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\n\t\t\t\t// Even if the snapshot applied under a different term, its\n\t\t\t\t// application is still valid. Snapshots carry committed\n\t\t\t\t// (term-independent) state.\n\t\t\t\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t// ignore other cases\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [term: %d] ignored a %s message with lower term from %x [term: %d]\",\n\t\t\t\tr.id, r.Term, m.Type, m.From, m.Term)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tswitch m.Type {\n\tcase pb.MsgHup:\n\t\tif r.preVote {\n\t\t\tr.hup(campaignPreElection)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tr.hup(campaignElection)\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgStorageAppendResp:\n\t\tif m.Index != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.raftLog.stableTo(entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index})\n\t\t}\n\t\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\n\t\t\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\n\t\t}\nfunc (u *unstable) stableTo(id entryID) {\n\tgt, ok := u.maybeTerm(id.index)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\t// Unstable entry missing. Ignore.\n\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at index %d missing from unstable log; ignoring\", id.index)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif id.index < u.offset {\n\t\t// Index matched unstable snapshot, not unstable entry. Ignore.\n\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at index %d matched unstable snapshot; ignoring\", id.index)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif gt != id.term {\n\t\t// Term mismatch between unstable entry and specified entry. Ignore.\n\t\t// This is possible if part or all of the unstable log was replaced\n\t\t// between that time that a set of entries started to be written to\n\t\t// stable storage and when they finished.\n\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at (index,term)=(%d,%d) mismatched with \"+\n\t\t\t\"entry at (%d,%d) in unstable log; ignoring\", id.index, id.term, id.index, gt)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tnum := int(id.index + 1 - u.offset)\n\tu.entries = u.entries[num:]\n\tu.offset = id.index + 1\n\tu.offsetInProgress = max(u.offsetInProgress, u.offset)\n\tu.shrinkEntriesArray()\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nartifact='017cd81f455948f2a0d0832a53e904e6';run='e365efbbde80420bb1b1730a6c13d88a'\nitems=[dict(aspect='applicability',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S_completion_contract','S_stable_contract','S_config','S_ready','S_election'],rationale='Reviewed Claim C_stale_append_completion version 1 and the fixed version-1 artifact basis. S_completion_contract (rawnode.go 315-321) explicitly promises no unstable-log truncation when the issuing Raft term changed; S_stable_contract explains why retirement needs assurance against pending overwrite. This is a documented implementation contract, not a universal necessary condition for every safe storage implementation. The fixed harness enables AsyncStorageWrites, delivers the original MsgStorageAppendResp only after actual ordered MemoryStorage operations, and establishes the earlier issuing term independently. The selected no-crash MemoryStorage execution is applicable to response-filter semantics: persistence survives the entire execution interval, while no disk/crash guarantee is claimed. Snapshot handling is deliberately excluded because S_election makes its completion term-independent.',limitations=['The obligation is intentionally narrower than absence of data loss: a particular old completion could be harmless, but still falls under the implementation\\\\'s documented conservative filter.','No disk durability or restart behavior is exercised.']),dict(aspect='decomposition',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S_ready','S_election','S_unstable','S_log_apply','S_config'],rationale='S_ready captures issuing Raft term separately from tail Index/LogTerm. S_election filters the context before S_unstable checks entry identity and removes a prefix. Both guards are meaningful: index/log-term matching alone is insufficient for the source-described overwrite concern, while the term filter alone does not validate arbitrary entry identities. The check isolates the context guard by observing unchanged tail identity. The actual term transition is supplied by a genuine rejected vote request, not a hand-assigned term. The current-term HardState-only response in the same execution records offset 5 -> 6 as a diagnostic permitted control. Neither that observation nor the monitored old-response comparison proves general eventual reclamation. Broader history inconsistency could still arise from wrong worker ordering, another writer, faulty reconstruction or application misuse while this obligation holds; these are not silently included in the checked proposition.',limitations=['No competing overwrite or complete source-comment ABA trajectory is executed.','Current-term control is a raw attributed observation rather than an independently monitored liveness obligation.']),dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S_api','S_bootstrap','S_transition','S_roles','S_proposal','S_receive','S_ready','S_election','S_unstable','S_config','S_mem_append','S_mem_hardstate','S_completion_contract','S_stable_contract'],rationale='Inspected the saved direct-checks/9fc4b62618184d41988fa5ce0bc8dfad/plan.json and assurance_generated_test.go, the version-1 claim and all three binding excerpts, CheckRun e365efbbde80420bb1b1730a6c13d88a, and its stdout/stderr. The harness constructs three real RawNodes from empty MemoryStorage, bootstraps/applies peer entries, elects node 1 and commits/applies its initial entry, then Proposes the measured tail. Actual emitted MsgApp and MsgVote messages produce node 2\\\\'s tail and term transition; no protocol fields are assigned. FIFO storage jobs perform actual Append/SetHardState before returning each original response. Vote rejection, self acknowledgments and later delayed network messages are retained and processed; finite omission of ticks cannot interfere with the immediately bracketed Step call. The trusted raw log shows prefix committed/applied 4 at term 2; batch 5 token (Term=2, Index=5, LogTerm=2); actual node-3 vote request at term 3; completed batch 5; admission with current term 3, offset 5, matching identity and no snapshot; and result offset 5 after actual Step. Monitor admission_alias is explicitly admitted. Prerequisite references require token production before transition/write and both before admission, and operation/node identify the single measured operation independently of offset or changing term. The actual predicate is result.offset == admitted.offset, with no result-offset applicability filter. S_unstable shows that prefix retirement would advance this offset; the selected entry-only Step branch cannot legitimately move it backward or replace it. Thus equality measures the accepted no-retirement responsibility without assuming the result. The runner matched prerequisites 0-4, evaluated result event 5, found no parsing errors, and reported a complete holds comparison. The same execution then observes the permitted term-3 control advancing offset to 6 and drains the scheduler to empty queues; completion does not wait for the forbidden behavior. No correspondence issue found for this one fully observed schedule.',limitations=['One unchanged-tail schedule with a vote-request term transition; no exhaustive schedule or configuration coverage.','Internal unstable offset is the endpoint, not public client completion or committed-data preservation.','MemoryStorage worker completion is scoped to this serialized no-crash execution.','No model equivalence, calibration, independent consensus vote, or overall correctness is established.'])]\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=artifact,rationale='Review the exact saved artifact and executed history as a bounded implementation-contract comparison; retain the wider history and application limits.',review_items=items,feedback=dict(ref_ids=[artifact,run,'S_completion_contract','S_election','S_unstable','S_membership','S_responses','S_read_release'],answered='The trusted run reached the selected stale-completion condition and measured offset 5 before and after the old term-2 response in term 3. The actual producer, legal bootstrap/election/replication prefix, same-history term transition, ordered storage completion and observed local endpoint are all present for this schedule. The later term-3 control retired the same tail (offset 6). The review finds no checker-correspondence issue for the accepted local requirement; this remains a bounded holds result, not a general proof.',remaining=['No further repair is identified for the measured old-token proposition. Competing overwrites, crash recovery and application consequences remain independent limits.','Next inspect the connection between configuration-driven maybeCommit and ReadIndex requests waiting for first current-term commit; determine the actual queue consumers and applicable completion contract before forming another Candidate.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='Return to the accepted overview/frontier after the local result. Repeating the stale guard with more disclaimers adds less than an independent consumer path. A full overwrite history would deepen the same protection but require a longer multi-leader prefix; ReadIndex queue lifetime has client consequence but an unread completion contract; configuration activation already reuses retained matches and invokes maybeCommit without the acknowledgment branch\\\\'s explicit pending-read release. Prefer reading that concrete connection next, preserving this completed measurement and without assuming the asymmetry is a defect.',question_updates={'45d41e2405de4b028bd8a31a7e3fc9b0':dict(unknowns=['One schedule does not cover competing overwrites, other term-transition paths, snapshot completion, crashes or application endpoints.'],resume_conditions=['Resume this proposition only if a new interfering writer, corrected source meaning or a concrete execution gap challenges its sco